Dear Samuel,

Thank you for reporting your experience.

I do not have access to Mountain Lion and cannot fully support it.
But if you are to compile with macports system, then
the right way is to use the libpq that accompany PostgreSQL like
all other unix systems, rather than tweeking the flags in libpq
subdirectory.  Probably, this can be suppressed by removing 
@ENABLE_LIBPQ@ from Makevars.in. 

The current setup is made to allow compilation on the CRAN
binary package making machine, which runs ver 10.5.8.
The standard binary distribution of R for Mac OS X should run on 
Mountain Lion without any problem, to my understanding.

-- 
